      "name": "InitializeGameState",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes core game state by loading global configuration data and applying settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize game object at address 0x103e0aac with size 8\n2. Load 7 data blocks (16 bytes each) from fixed memory addresses:\n   - Block 1 from 0x1029a3f0 (offset 0x8)\n   - Block 2 from 0x1029a390 (offset 0x18)\n   - Block 3 from 0x1029a3a0 (offset 0x2c)\n   - Block 4 from 0x1029a420 (offset 0x40)\n   - Block 5 from 0x1029a430 (offset 0x50)\n   - Block 6 from 0x1029a4d0 (offset 0x60)\n   - Block 7 from 0x1029a4e0 (offset 0x70)\n3. Set magic validation values 0x474 and 0x475 in stack frame\n4. Call FUN_101719f0 to process loaded data configuration\n5. Call FUN_10171d30 to finalize game object state\n6. Call FUN_10233b13 to apply global settings from 0x102457a0\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs initialization side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic values 0x474 and 0x475 are validation markers for data block processing\n- All data blocks are copied via XMM registers for optimized alignment\n- Function uses __stdcall convention with callee cleanup",
