      "name": "InitializeGraphicsDevice",
      "signature": "void InitializeGraphicsDevice(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the graphics device by configuring device driver names and calling initialization routines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize global graphics data structure to zero\n2. Populate a local array with 9 device driver name identifiers (DWORD values encoding device names)\n3. Call graphics library initialization routine with driver names and temporary buffer\n4. Configure the primary graphics device with initialized settings\n5. Finalize graphics device setup and establish device context\n6. Register graphics device with the application system\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nNone (void function)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Device names are stored as ASCII-encoded DWORD values in little-endian format\n- Function performs no error checking; relies on called functions for validation\n- Global graphics data at DAT_103e0b4c is reset and reinitialized\n- Function uses __stdcall convention with 0x30 bytes of local stack space\n\nStructure Layout:\nDevice Name Identifiers (little-endian ASCII):\nOffset | Size | Value      | Decoded   | Purpose\n-------|------|------------|-----------|------------------\n0x00   | 4    | 0x6f686364 | \"dcho\"    | Device identifier 1\n0x04   | 4    | 0x6f736364 | \"dsco\"    | Device identifier 2\n0x08   | 4    | 0x6c626364 | \"dbcl\"    | Device identifier 3\n0x0C   | 4    | 0x766d7472 | \"rmtv\"    | Device identifier 4\n0x10   | 4    | 0x6f6d7472 | \"rmto\"    | Device identifier 5\n0x14   | 4    | 0x66326d63 | \"cm2f\"    | Device identifier 6\n0x18   | 4    | 0x6263756c | \"lucb\"    | Device identifier 7\n0x1C   | 4    | 0x6363756c | \"lucc\"    | Device identifier 8\n0x20   | 4    | 0x6463756c | \"lucd\"    | Device identifier 9",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
