      "name": "InitializeSkillData",
      "signature": "void InitializeSkillData(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes skill data by registering skill names with the game system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize skill data structure via FUN_101718e0 with global DAT_103e0b44\n2. Fill local buffer with 23 skill names encoded as little-endian DWORD values\n3. Call FUN_101719f0 to process skill names from buffer\n4. Extract processed values from returned structure (offsets +0 and +4)\n5. Call FUN_10171cb0 to register processed skill data\n6. Call FUN_10233b13 to finalize skill initialization with 0x102457f0 parameter\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - Uses global skill data structure DAT_103e0b44\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Skill names are stored as little-endian encoded DWORD values\n- Local buffer contains 23 skill names used in D2 game\n- Names include: bks, dkb, dhm, 1rt, ass, box, msf, vip, tsh, j33, q33, zyx, yeq, hqr, bqr, 1fq, 2fq, bbb, ssm, hfh, eci, 2rt, and trailing spaces\n- Stack is 16-byte aligned before SUB ESP,0x68 to maintain calling convention",
