      "name": "InitializeGameData",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameData(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes game data structures by loading configuration blocks from global memory and preparing them for processing.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Call FUN_101718a0 with DAT_103e0b2c and size 8 (initialize primary data source)\\n2. Load four 16-byte data blocks from global memory addresses:\\n   - Block 1: 0x10299f70-0x10299f7c (dataBlock4)\\n   - Block 2: 0x1029a220-0x1029a22c (dataBlock3)\\n   - Block 3: 0x1029a2d0-0x1029a2dc (dataBlock2)\\n   - Block 4: 0x1029a350-0x1029a35c (dataBlock1)\\n3. Call FUN_101719f0 to process the loaded data blocks (copies data into local buffers)\\n4. Call FUN_10171d30 to finalize initialization of DAT_103e0b2c\\n5. Call FUN_10233b13(0x10245800) to complete data setup or registration\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone - Function takes no explicit parameters\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - No return value\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Uses XMM instructions (MOVAPS/MOVUPS) for 128-bit aligned data transfers\\n- Stack is aligned to 8-byte boundary before operations (AND ESP,0xfffffff8)\\n- Loads global data into local stack buffers (16-byte blocks) before processing\\n- The magic address 0x10245800 passed to final function may represent a game state pointer or configuration handle",
