      "name": "InitializeGameLevelAreas",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameLevelAreas(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize all Diablo II game level area data structures\n\nThis function sets up the game world by initializing 38 level area buffers with\ntheir descriptions and configuration data. It performs exception handling setup\nand cleanup around the initialization process and calls supporting functions to\nregister and configure the level data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up exception handling frame with exception list linkage\n2. Initialize arena context pointer (DAT_103e0a88)\n3. Initialize 38 level area buffers sequentially (one per level/area)\n4. Each level receives a FUN_10171e10 call with area string and ID (0x0-0x25)\n5. Register initialized level data structures using FUN_101719f0\n6. Register level data pointers using FUN_10171bd0\n7. Flush and commit all area data using FUN_102336f9\n8. Register game data table using FUN_10233b13\n9. Restore exception handling state and return\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, initializes global game structures as side effects\n\nParameters:\nNone - No input parameters, operates on global game state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses structured exception handling with canary value verification\n- XOR canary stored in exceptionState, XORed with EBP for corruption detection\n- Stack space: 0x398 bytes (920 bytes) allocated for 38 level buffers\n- Each level buffer is 24 bytes in size, initialized in descending stack order\n- Area IDs range from 0x0 (Blood Moor/Den of Evil) to 0x25 (Worldstone Keep)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:67428d6e18e61b028143d87a8b32bf85",
