      "name": "InitializeGameSystems",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameSystems(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes all core game systems and subsystems at startup.\n\nThis is the main initialization entry point that sets up:\n- Core game engine state (via FUN_101718e0)\n- Multiple game system parameters through FUN_101725a0 calls\n- Game resource initialization\n- Final system startup procedures\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push stack frame and align ESP to 8-byte boundary\n2. Call core engine initialization with game state pointer\n3. Initialize 7 system parameter pairs with specific ID/size combinations\n4. Initialize 3 global reference parameters\n5. Call secondary initialization routine with local buffers\n6. Finalize game state\n7. Load primary game resource\n8. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no parameters, executes on fixed global state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number values (0x13, 0xd, 0xf, 0x10, 0x12) represent system IDs\n- Global references are core game structures\n- Must be called during game initialization before gameplay\n- Stack aligned to 8-byte boundary for SSE compatibility",
