      "signature": "void InitializeEncryptionContext(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes encryption context with cipher keys and execution state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize encryption context state via InitializeEncryptionState()\n2. Setup cipher key material in local stack buffer:\n   - cipherKey0 = 0x41503033 (\"0PA\" ASCII encoding)\n   - cipherKey1 = 0x32484754 (\"TGH2\" ASCII encoding)\n   - cipherKey2 = 0x57375258 (\"X2W7\" ASCII encoding)\n3. Execute key scheduling/initialization via ProcessCipherKeys()\n   passing buffer and cipher key material\n4. Finalize encryption state via FinalizeEncryptionState()\n5. Apply encryption operation via ApplyEncryption() with data address 0x10245870\n\nReturns:\nNone (void return type). Side effects: modifies global encryption state\nand applies cipher operations to target data region.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses hardcoded magic values derived from ASCII encoding\n- Stack-based key material: 12 bytes total (3 DWORDs)\n- Direct data address reference: 0x10245870 suggests static data encryption",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
