      "name": "InitializeCipherData",
      "signature": "void InitializeCipherData(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes cipher data structures and processes encryption configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_101718a0 with size parameter (8 bytes) to initialize global cipher state\n2. Load configuration values 0x8f and 0x6b into local variables\n3. Copy global cipher data (8 bytes) from 0x10299eb0 using XMM register\n4. Copy three additional 4-byte global values from adjacent memory locations\n5. Call FUN_101719f0 to process/transform cipher configuration with local data\n6. Call FUN_10171d30 to finalize cipher state using global state pointer\n7. Call FUN_10233b13 with callback address 0x102467f0 for post-initialization\n8. Return void\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses XMM0 register and MOVUPS for unaligned data transfer (suggests 128-bit cipher blocks)\n- Configuration values 0x8f and 0x6b appear to be cipher parameters or mode flags\n- Global data at 0x10299eb0-0x10299ebc (16 bytes total) contains cipher key or state\n- Called as data reference from 0x102563a8 (likely initialization callback table)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2d6a6cc173ee74f204c9b31fa8b8f49f",
