      "name": "InitializeGamePreferences",
      "signature": "void InitializeGamePreferences(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes all game preferences and graphics settings from configuration data.\\nThis function sets up 26 different preference categories including audio settings\\n(sound mixer, master volume, music volume), game options (NPC speech, positional bias),\\ngraphics settings (perspective, light quality, shadows, contrast), automap options\\n(centers, party, fade, mode, position, left display), and UI settings (HP/MP text,\\npopup hiring, always run, mini panel, skip to open, max players, difficulty level).\\nEach setting is initialized by calling the appropriate configuration function with its\\nconfiguration data pointer and setting name string.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Set up SEH (Structured Exception Handling) frame for exception protection\\n2. Initialize each of 26 game settings in sequence (indices 0-25):\\n   - Create configuration object with setting data and name string\\n   - Call appropriate config function (FUN_10193540 for most, FUN_10193570/101935b0/101935e0 for variants)\\n3. Post-process the first configuration (index 0) with FUN_101719f0\\n4. Clean up and finalize with FUN_1018f770\\n5. Register exception handler with FUN_102336f9\\n6. Finalize with FUN_10233b13\\n7. Restore exception list and return\\n\\nParameters: None (no parameters)\\nReturns: void (no return value)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention with callee cleanup\\n- All 26 settings are created with sequential index values 0-25\\n- Exception handling protects the entire initialization sequence\\n- Each setting references a specific global configuration data structure\\n- Buffer sizes are all 28 bytes (0x1c) for configuration objects",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f48748a15f187ed353eecf1251222e4f",
