      "name": "InitializeConfigRegistry",
      "signature": "void InitializeConfigRegistry(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the configuration registry with network, account, and game settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up exception handling with SEH (Structured Exception Handling) frame\n2. Initialize network adapter configuration with address 0x103e4bc8\n3. Set TCP/IP address from default string \"216.148.246.35\"\n4. Load last used TCP/IP preference from registry key \"lasttcpip\"\n5. Load preferred realm from registry key \"preferred_realm\"\n6. Load last Battle.net account from registry key \"last_bnet\"\n7. Initialize profile version settings from key 0x103e4bf8\n8. Load save path preference from registry key \"save_path\"\n9. Load default channel preference from registry key \"default_channel\"\n10. Register all configuration entries with settings manager\n11. Execute post-initialization callbacks\n12. Clean up and restore exception handling frame\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Initialization routine with no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs side effects only (initializes global state)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exception handler value 0xffffffff indicates initial exception state\n- Each configuration buffer is 28 bytes (0x1c), allocated on local stack\n- Configuration state tracked in byte at [EBP-0x4] (0-7 indicate stage)\n- Registry keys are paired with string data for default values\n- Function modifies global exception handling chain via ExceptionList\n- All configuration keys pre-defined at fixed addresses in data segment",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f4c687b4e5b4eea42923e3e371b0aa5b",
