      "name": "InvokeGameInitializationCallback",
      "signature": "void InvokeGameInitializationCallback(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Invokes a game initialization callback routine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EBP register on stack\n2. Set up stack frame\n3. Push saved return address as parameter\n4. Call the actual initialization handler function\n5. Restore stack and return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  None (implicit: caller's return address passed to handler)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - This is a thin wrapper function that passes control to FUN_101b0a70\n  - The return address from caller is repurposed as an argument to handler\n  - Part of a callback/dispatch table (referenced from data at 0x102620d0)",
